  "verbalization": "Eribulin is implicated in the inhibition of microtubules, a mechanism that is shared with docetaxel and ibabepilone, both of which bind to Tubb8. The shared microtubule inhibition pathway suggests a potential mechanism by which Eribulin exerts its effects on Tubb8. The lowest common ancestor of Eribulin and its related compounds points to a common functional category, the \"Tubulin Binding Agent,\" which supports the notion of a shared biological target. The evidence from these paths indicates that Eribulin may act through a microtubule-dependent mechanism that involves Tubb8, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of a common ancestor in the \"Ketone\" category adds a layer of biochemical context, suggesting that the compounds may share a common metabolic pathway, which could influence their biological activity.",
